<title>FRANCE: French adj April current a/c surplus 23.8 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French adj April current a/c surplus 23.8 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's current account showed a seasonally adjusted surplus of 23.8 billion francs in April, a sharp increase from an unrevised 9.37 billion surplus in March, the Economy Ministry said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Ministry said the seasonally adjusted surplus in the first four months of 1997 was 73.36 billion francs, compared with a 32.36 billion surplus in the first four months of 1996.  </p>
<p>Detailed figures in billions of francs showed (unadjusted unless stated):</p>
<p>					April     March February</p>
<p> Current account (adjusted)   23.76     9.37    19.23</p>
<p> Current account		  20.27    14.92    10.42</p>
<p> Merchandise trade		17.11    15.62     9.98</p>
<p> Services			    8.30     7.47     2.00</p>
<p> Other goods and services	0.00     0.00     0.00</p>
<p> Income			     -3.12    -4.12     6.09</p>
<p> Transfers			  -2.03    -4.05    -7.64</p>
<p>The ministry also gave the following seasonally adjusted data on the current account in billions of francs:</p>
<p>					April    March    April 96</p>
<p> Current account		  23.76     9.37     7.83</p>
<p> Merchandise trade		14.39    12.34     2.99</p>
<p> Services			    7.40     6.08     5.93</p>
<p>  -Travel			    4.95     5.44     4.14</p>
<p> Other goods and services	0.00     0.00     0.00</p>
<p> Income				1.16     0.63     1.09</p>
<p>  -Investment income	     0.03     0.11     0.03</p>
<p> Transfers			  -2.30    -3.93    -5.61</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
